From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenBook <noreply@anybook.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: microG signature spoofing in user builds too

LineageOS's "Allow signature spoofing for microG Companion/Services" only
spoofs on debuggable (userdebug/eng) builds. OpenBook ships microG as an
optional add-on on user builds as well (ANAL-210), so drop that one
condition, as lineageos4microg does for its user builds. Every other
condition stays:
* the package is com.google.android.gms or com.android.vending;
* it is signed with microG's release certificate (SHA-256
  9bd06727e62796c0130eb6dab39b73157451582cbd138e86c468acc395d14165) and
  nothing else;
* the fake signature it asks for is exactly Google's platform-services
  certificate.

The isDebuggable() JNI method stays declared, so the LineageOS commit
underneath applies unchanged.
---
 services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/ComputerEngine.java | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/ComputerEngine.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/ComputerEngine.java
index f84f36cb90af..084b8835d0c6 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/ComputerEngine.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/ComputerEngine.java
@@ -1492,9 +1492,8 @@ public class ComputerEngine implements Computer {
     private static native boolean isDebuggable();
 
     public static boolean isMicrogSigned(AndroidPackage p) {
-        if (!isDebuggable()) {
-            return false;
-        }
+        // OpenBook: no isDebuggable() condition, so that user builds behave like userdebug ones. The package names,
+        // microG's release certificate and the one fake signature below still have to match.
 
         // Allowlist the following apps:
         // * com.android.vending - microG Companion
